From: Herrie <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] platform: msm8953: include arch/defines.h for dmb()

dmb() is a macro from arch/defines.h which platform.c only picked up
implicitly with older toolchains. GCC 14 promotes
-Wimplicit-function-declaration to an error, breaking the build:

  platform/msm8953/platform.c:101:9: error: implicit declaration of
  function 'dmb' [-Wimplicit-function-declaration]

Include the header explicitly.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 platform/msm8953/platform.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/platform/msm8953/platform.c
+++ b/platform/msm8953/platform.c
@@ -29,5 +29,6 @@
 #include <debug.h>
 #include <reg.h>
+#include <arch/defines.h>
 #include <platform/iomap.h>
 #include <platform/irqs.h>
 #include <platform/clock.h>
